WEBVTT

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.470
Yesterday was rough, huh?

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.810
Yeah.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:21.980
But we can't sit back and relax, or
Sentucky might take our customers again.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:28.820
No way do we want to go to Greenland, right, substitute manager Sadao Maou?

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:31.990
Maa!

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.610
Go out to Hushimaen tomorrow.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.660
What?!

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.200
Why?! I made our sales goal like you said!

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.290
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.080
A girl from my year who manages the MgR's there

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:46.880
asked me to lend her one of my top workers.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:48.210
Phew, you scared me.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.720
There'll be a big crowd at the park tomorrow,

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.720
since they're opening new attractions and having a fair and stuff.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:58.390
We'll cover expenses and give you a bonus for the trouble, obviously.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.060
Well? Will you do it?

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:01.100
Of course.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:02.680
I'll help, too!

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:06.100
It's okay, Maa's the only one we need.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:06.900
Oh...

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:11.110
--Well, then, I'm counting on you to do this right as my top crew member.
--Hushimaen, huh?

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:11.990
Understood.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:27.540
<i>Kono shunkan, kono basho ga sutaato</i>

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:33.590
<i>Imeeji shite miyou naniga dekiru no ka na</i>

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:37.550
<i>Shinjirarenai dekigoto datte aru</i>

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:43.270
<i>Motto... koete yukeru ne</i>

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:54.240
<i>Zero kara umareru subete kagayaite ano sora e</i>

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.700
<i>Omoikiri habatakitai</i>

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:05.830
<i>Saikou no sumairu de warainagara saa yukou!</i>

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:11.670
<i>Michi no sekai e to ima tobidasou yo</i>

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.340
<i>Mirai wo erabi, kimeru no wa jibun</i>

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.640
<i>Yume wo oikakete yukou</i>

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.260
<i>Naku hi mo aru</i>

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:26.520
<i>Sore wa daiji na negai, kienaide</i>

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:34.440
<i>Kitto aeru kara, asu no kimi e...</i>

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.000
Hmm? Tomorrow?

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.210
Yeah.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:56.630
You're eatin' too much. You're not totally recovered, so don't overdo it.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.300
But Sire...

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:04.260
The noodles will expire soon, so we need to finish them in the next day or two.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:06.430
I am grateful for your concern.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.810
Hey, she's right.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:11.690
There's a new haunted house opening at Hushimaen tomorrow,

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.440
and there's some "Great Asian
Reptile Exhibit" thing starting too.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:18.440
Quit web-surfing and start eating.
We need to get this done.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.530
There's gonna be 300 reptile species all in one place.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:23.570
I bet this'll bring in a ton of visitors.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.410
It sounds like you'll have a hard day's work.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:26.120
Yep.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.750
Huh, the new haunted house

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.540
is supposed to be scarier than
Aso-Q Lowland's Labyrinth of Shocks,

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:34.290
and people call that the scariest in Japan.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:38.970
So, if a crowd of people is coming to a crazy-scary haunted house...

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:44.180
Doesn't it figure that there'd be a big concentration of human fear?

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.810
You might be able to collect some magic.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:53.440
In that case, I, Ashiya, shall accompany Your Highness tomorrow

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.400
and assist you with furious zeal.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.690
Hmm, so you're going too.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.450
Yes, I am.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:01.950
Hmm.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.160
You stay here and behave yourself.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.030
What?

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.040
Food money. I'm ordering pizza.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.250
I will not allow such extravagance! You eat udon!

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.960
Oh, but don't you mess with the kitchen.
I'll make your food tonight.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:20.920
You sure that udon isn't getting sketchy, freshness-wise?

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.590
It's still plenty good.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.640
If you don't eat it, the
Wastefulness Ghosts will get you.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:30.480
Are you stupid?

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.770
How dare you!

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:32.520
Ugh, gross!

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:36.150
Whatever, hurry up and eat!
We gotta get this done!

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:42.650
Hello. Chiho?

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.530
Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.120
Huh? Hushimaen?

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.160
Sure, that's fine. I'm free tomorrow anyway.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.120
Um, thank you!

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:57.590
I'm so glad you're coming with me, Miss Yusa.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.630
Going all alone would just be weird.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.380
Right! Let's meet there.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.180
I really wanted to go with Mr. Maou, but...

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:15.730
Hello?

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:19.770
The Devil is planning to collect magic tomorrow at Hushimaen.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:24.070
What? I thought he was just helping out another MgRonald's.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.360
Word has already reached you, Emilia?

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.280
I heard it from Chiho.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:32.540
I'm going to Hushimaen, too, actually. She invited me.

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:36.120
And "collecting"-- Isn't the place an amusement park?

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.670
Where do you see this going?

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:43.210
You're never suspicious enough.
I want to assess the situation in person.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.340
I'd like you to take me with you.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:50.300
Okay. I'll let Chiho know you're coming along.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:56.270
Why does Emilia...?

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:02.940
I'm Sadao Maou, from the Hatagaya MgR's.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.400
I'm pleased to meet you!

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:09.780
Kisaki's told me about you.
She says you're good.

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.490
I'll strive to live up to your expectations, Ma'am.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:16.410
Okay, today's going to be a busy day, so everybody bring your A game!

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:17.580
Yes, Ma'am!

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.300
Miss Yusa!

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:28.130
Sorry, did we keep you waiting?

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:31.890
No, not at all. Hello, Miss Suzuno!

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:35.310
Good Chiho, I put myself in your care.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.850
This is my first visit to an amusement park,

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.190
so I'd like you to teach me its ways.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.940
Leave it to me!

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:48.610
Here I am!

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:53.530
Two Special One-Pound Burgers, all ready!

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:58.120
Wow, Miss Yusa, you're so adult!

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:01.380
Two MgBurgers, all ready!

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.790
Listen, Chiho...

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:03.540
Yes?

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:06.760
You're sixteen right now, right...?

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:08.090
That's right!

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:11.340
--Dammit...
--Is something wrong?

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:16.310
Huh? Oh, it's just, you're so big--I mean, cute!

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:18.770
Really?!

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:21.560
I wonder if Mr. Maou will think so, too!

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:24.770
Here I am.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:30.360
Well, shall we go?

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.450
What's wrong, you two?

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.540
Thank you very much!

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:40.370
Next customer, please!

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:43.880
Two nuggets, one barbeque sauce, one mustard sauce,

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:46.670
one iced caramel latte, one café mocha,

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:51.180
and two MgBurgers, one without pickles, please!

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.850
Thank you very much!

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.760
You're good.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:07:59.730
Next customer, please!

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:00.600
Huh?

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:02.020
Chi!

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:04.150
Hello, Mr. Maou.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:07.650
Three Big Mag meals, please!

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:11.110
Will that be all, Miss?

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.320
Yes.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:14.870
Three Big Mag meals, please!

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.740
I came to hang out at the park.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:17.830
Oh, you did?

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:20.120
Good luck today, Mr. Maou!

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:21.540
Thanks.

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:23.370
Um...

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.290
What do you think?

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:27.840
About what?

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:33.340
Oh! Well, this park branch is a lot busier than our neighborhood one.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:37.350
There's a ton of customers, so it'll be good service practice for me.

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:38.850
Yes, of course.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.480
I gotta report to Miss Kisaki when I get back!

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:45.020
Yes, of course... I sort of knew this would happen.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:47.110
You've got zero delicacy.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:50.070
What are <i>you</i> two doing here?

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:54.780
We hardworking OLs are free to do whatever we want on our days off, aren't we?

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:55.950
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:59.990
And I am not here for pleasure.
I am learning about society.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.500
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:13.300
You okay? You sure you didn't eat too much udon?

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:16.220
This is... nothing at all...

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:18.390
You sure you shouldn't take some meds?

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:22.100
No one takes medicine for a little stomach... ache...!

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:26.940
I'm so ashamed...

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:29.980
I intended to devote myself to assisting King Satan

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:34.990
in his magic collection, and now look at my sorry state...

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.910
You sure you shouldn't take it easy for a while?

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.950
And if you're at home anyway,

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:43.200
either just stay in there or stay in bed.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:47.290
Hey, you okay?

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:51.500
Wow, this place is really crowded!

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:55.510
I guess they're here for the new attraction?

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.720
You mean the haunted house?

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.510
Yes--the rumor says it's pretty intense!

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:02.310
Want to go check it out?

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:03.470
By all means.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:05.770
You might be able to collect some magic.

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:11.270
I have several reasons to be interested.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:38.510
Let's go.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:40.680
Huh? Um...

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:56.940
--Chiho?!
--Good Chiho?!

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:03.450
Sheesh, how far did Chiho run?

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:06.120
She must have made it quite far ahead of us.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:19.180
Is that--no, it's not Chiho.

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:23.760
Hello, child, what's wrong? Why are you crying?

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:24.930
She's gone.

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:27.180
"Gone"? Who's gone?

00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:28.680
Mom.

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:30.140
Did you get split up?

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:31.270
She's gone!

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:35.270
I see. Do you want to come with us, then?

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:38.070
She's gone. Mom's gone.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:40.280
She's gone. She's gon--

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:44.370
She's gone. Mom's go-- She's go-gone.

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:48.580
--Sh-She's Mom's Mom gone Mo go she's gone Mom's gone gone Mo--

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:48.580
--H-Hey...

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:54.040
Oh, it's Mom.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:02.300
Who thought that up?!

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:06.060
I really thought I had the stomach for that sort of thing...

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.350
Shall we try that one next?

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:17.270
Chi-Chiho? It's not too late to turn back...

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:19.400
I-I'll go! I'll go!

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:22.490
Really? I honestly don't mind if we don't...

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.370
No, we came all this way, so I'm going!

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:27.740
You're sure?

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:30.540
Perhaps <i>you're</i> afraid, good Emi?

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:35.250
Excuse me? <i>Afraid</i>?!
I just don't <i>like</i> them much, that's all!

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:37.250
I don't like them either.

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:47.220
It's creepy when they just appear out of nowhere...

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.060
Yeah, it is...

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:04.030
I really don't like them...

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:05.660
Me either...

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:09.120
Still, it seems there are many different types here.

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.040
Do they have edible ones?

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:14.170
"Edible"? Wait, have you eaten them before?!

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:15.580
Yes, a few times.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:18.040
What?! Where?!

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:21.050
As I recall, it was on a trip south.

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:22.300
To Okinawa?

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:25.880
--You're sure to regret it if you don't eat lizard meat before you leave!

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:23.970
--An acquaintance there

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:25.890
--told me that I was sure to regret it

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:29.640
--We use everything from head to tail! Please, eat!

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:28.390
--if I didn't eat lizard meat before I left.

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:29.640
--Did you have no choice?

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:33.390
I was reluctant at first, but she was so adamant...

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:35.440
You... ate it, didn't you.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:40.440
The inn prided itself on using every part, from head to tail.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:44.030
I must say, the lizard-tail soup was particularly superb.

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:48.780
The broth was good, naturally, but really it was quite delicious overall.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:52.160
--It looked grotesque, but that didn't even bother me.
--H-Hold on!

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:54.460
It might well be Ente Is--

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:00.500
Why are you telling Chiho about Ente Isla?!

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:02.130
I've misstepped...

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:05.550
--Maou!
--Yes?

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:08.010
Make the in-park deliveries when you're done with those, okay?

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:09.220
Yes, Ma'am!

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:34.790
Whoa!

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.330
Oh, excuse me.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:38.580
No, no, excuse me!

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:40.330
No, it was my fault.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:43.670
What?

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:45.880
You're cute, Miss Yusa.

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:47.300
Jeez!

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:50.390
MgRonald's delivery! I have your order here!

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:54.310
Ah, we've been waiting for this!
Would you mind carrying it inside?

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:57.180
Now, this one is the Big Mag, and--

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:11.320
This is amazing. I had no idea there were so many types!

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:12.830
Me either!

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:15.910
So, see any of the kind you ate?

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:20.000
Well, I've been trying not to look at them from that perspective...

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.210
Hmm?

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:23.290
This monkey...

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:26.630
Could he be lost? He's wearing clothes...

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:29.800
Hey, don't be scared, come on out.

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:41.980
This monkey kinda pisses me off.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:44.440
Thank you and please order MgRonald's again!

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:46.530
Huh? Sadao!

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:47.570
Sadao?

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:49.700
Right, he's my little monkey.

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.950
Monkey, huh?

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:54.120
Sadao!

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:56.040
Where the heck did he go?

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.790
Hey, Sadao!

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:01.250
Sadao! Where are you?

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:03.630
S-Sadao!

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:05.630
What should we do with him?

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:08.010
Why not take him to the Lost Children Center?

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:10.670
Sadao!

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:13.550
Sadao!

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:16.760
Now, Sadao, you know you can't go off on your own!

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:19.270
--Well, I'm glad you found him.
--Yeah!

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:21.140
Mr. Maou?

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.390
Hi, Chi!

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:24.400
Thanks, Miss, you're a lifesaver!

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:26.770
So this little guy's name is Sadao?

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:27.480
Yep!

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.440
Were you lost, Sadao?

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:32.860
Thank goodness you found your master, huh, Sadao?

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:37.160
Sadao here loves the ladies, you see. He's a real problem child!

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:40.000
Ah, yes... and he likes big ones best...

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:41.660
--"Big ones"?
--Um, never mind--

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:44.380
Just cut it out, you guys!

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.980
Whee!

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:09.730
Whee.

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:29.840
What is it?

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:33.550
I have an urgent message for all guests.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:36.930
Alligators have escaped from the reptile exhibit hall.

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:39.720
--Chiho!
--Please follow park employee instructions in evacuating the area.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:45.270
--I repeat: I have an urgent message for all guests.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.390
--Everyone please evacuate calmly!

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:45.270
--Don't get separated from your children!

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:48.860
--Alligators have escaped from the reptile exhibit hall.

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:46.900
--Are you okay, Chiho?

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:48.860
--Yes...

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:52.780
--Please follow park employee instructions in evacuating the area.

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:52.780
--Suzuno?

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:17.970
Unclean soul, return to me from the netherworld.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:21.680
Vanquish before me these weak-willed creatures.

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:27.850
Unclean soul, return to me from the netherworld.

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:31.270
Vanquish before me these weak-willed creatures.

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:35.440
Is that Mr. Maou?

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:37.110
Looks like it.

00:18:56.760 --> 00:19:01.890
Why? He could have taken advantage of the chaos to gain more power...

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:05.930
...but instead he's using what he collected to help the humans?

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:10.650
What's going on in your mind,
Satan, ruler of demons?

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.400
--Good night!
--'Night, everybody!

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:18.110
--Today was sure wild, huh?
--I know, right?!

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:21.320
You did even better work than Kisaki said you would!

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:24.120
Really? Thank you very much!

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:28.580
Well, I still have cleanup duty.
See you tomorrow at work, Chi.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:30.750
Yep, see you tomorrow!

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:35.800
Honestly, the way he pretended to be busy...

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:43.140
No, I think maybe today was worth it, just to see Mr. Maou being cool.

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:44.180
Okay then.

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:50.640
Plus, I got to have a blast with you two. That's enough for me!

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.560
Yeah, it was nice to finally rest and recharge!

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:54.610
Right?

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.780
Ah, yes, of course...

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:36.820
Miss Suzuno?

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:55.460
Oh, hey, did you get magic yesterday?

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:59.710
Mmm, hard to say whether
I got some or just used some up.

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:06.350
I knew anything Urushihara said... wasn't to be relied on...

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:10.520
I apologize for... interrupting your meal, Sire...

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:12.390
It's sorta painful to look at you.

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.940
It's... nothing to worry about...

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:16.360
Yeah, he just overate.

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:19.650
Quiet! None of that from you!

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:21.610
Special delivery!

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:23.740
--Coming!
--I'll get it--

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:26.280
Crap! My legs won't work!

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:29.700
--One second, be right there.
--W-Wait, I said I'd get it!

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:32.870
I have a delivery for Mr. Hanzo Urushihara.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:34.540
Urushihara?

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:35.790
Jungle...

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:38.290
U-Um, you see, this is...

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.090
--This is <i>what</i>?
--So close, so close, so close.

00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:41.510
Go on, tell me.

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:45.090
What did you do while I was living in the bathr--

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:48.100
Ashiya, wanna go to the clinic?

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:50.810
N-No need! It's nothing...!

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:51.970
You really okay?

00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:57.480
Shut up! I don't... want <i>you</i> worrying about me...!

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:23.550
<i>Doko kara asa ni naru? Shizuka na sora</i>

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:29.140
<i>Minai furi wo shita yubikiri koyubi no saki</i>

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:39.340
<i>Warawareta tsuki nara kiete</i> <i>yuku n da kinou no houkaku e</i>

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:45.280
<i>Usotsuki okubyoumono</i> <i>minna matomete boku nara</i>

00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:51.070
<i>Saite ita no wa yume no naka da</i>

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:56.540
<i>Tsuki no kage ni kakushiteta</i> <i>hontou wa ne naiteta</i>

00:22:56.750 --> 00:23:02.250
<i>Namida wa mou nagarenai karete shimatta no?</i>

00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:08.880
<i>Nani mo ka mo yurusetara</i> <i>nagareru ka mo shirenai kedo</i>

00:23:09.090 --> 00:23:16.430
<i>Mamoritai mono bakari da na</i>

00:23:38.370 --> 00:23:41.000
"The Hero Stays True to Her Convictions"
